; ted-outmem-blitz2-init-verreq (#1008): the requester case - blitz2
; opens its version requester through TED's openreq before TED's main
; loop; a window that cannot be opened is out of memory there (outmem,
; which continues with memstack = 0, a7 = 0).  blitz2 under inject
; (alerts answered), the OpenWindow of the version requester (the 2nd
; window of the process) fails; then CREATE EXECUTABLE, QUIT.  Correct:
; the alert "Not enough memory for operation!", the start goes on without
; the version requester, the compile creates the executable and blitz2
; ends normally; the original continues with a7 = 0 and crashes, blitz2
; 2.10 under TED-C waits for the version requester's gadget (hangs).  The
; first two waits are longer than the session (90 s): a hang ends as the
; crash does, a session timeout.
; @fixed-orig #1008 Cc
; @file bo.bas "NPrint \"hello\"\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts openwindowfail=2 blitz2:blitz2 @FILE@
; @expect stdout " windows asked for, 1 failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect stdout "inject: rc=0"
; @expect exists bo
timeout 120
wait screen
menu 4 2
wait freq "Name of Executable to create"
timeout 30
freq ok "bo" "TEDRUN:work"  ; @ignore compilewindow
timeout 10
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
